MuJoCo 3.14.0 + the upstream EPA horizon fix, limited to the horizon sizing and its bounds check.

Upstream commit: 6d662aedda693a1225a03a26c6b3ddd5e3cc4fbe
  "Add guard for max edges in EPA horizon, and change max edges to depend linearly on ccd_iterations. Print useful
   info on how much to increase ccd_iterations. Fixes #3646."  (Kyle Bayes, 2026-10-06; first released in 3.15.0)
  https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/6d662aedda693a1225a03a26c6b3ddd5e3cc4fbe
  https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/issues/3646

Taken: every src/engine/engine_collision_gjk.c hunk of that commit except one: the removal of the unused
`#include <mujoco/mjmodel.h>` (unrelated). Not taken: its test changes (test/engine/engine_collision_gjk_test.cc).
The hunks apply to the 3.14.0 tag (9ecbb9d7b5ee623f54745638d36799ff90e6f7cd) with line offsets only.

